    {
      "area": "Parent hierarchy and efficiency",
      "finding": "All five daily states have readable child identity, remaining/saved/available time, daily duration and renewal. Pause/Resume and exhausted Add minutes today are direct actions; the editor is a single accordion away. End now is visually distinct and separated from ordinary adjustments."
    },
    {
      "area": "Responsive layout",
      "finding": "All twenty state cards and four expanded editors fit without horizontal clipping at the four supplied widths. Phone stacks actions; portrait two-column cards wrap renewal text naturally; landscape and desktop place adjustments on one row. Mixed four-child pages retain recognizable per-child boundaries."
    },
    {
      "area": "Editor semantics",
      "finding": "Editor explicitly states daily starts when the child opens the library, unused time does not carry over, 1\u2013240 whole minutes, and background/paused-video wall-clock counting. Selected 5-minute duration is visibly emphasized; save includes the chosen duration. Renewal timezone and persistent Parent stops/pauses are disclosed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Child clarity",
      "finding": "Countdown is plainly visible above the library at all four widths. Exhausted and Parent-blocked screens are calm, readable and use different explanatory copy. Library/Ask Parent navigation and profile selection remain available; screenshot does not establish their behavior."
    },
    {
      "area": "Typography, spacing, icons and contrast",
      "finding": "Consistent lavender/navy palette, icon treatment, strong headings and generous card/action spacing. Core action rectangles appear touch sized. Secondary text remains readable visually; no measured WCAG contrast or programmatic target-size certification performed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Phone fixed navigation",
      "finding": "Phone Child full-page capture shows fixed bottom navigation across mid-document cards. This is consistent with viewport-fixed navigation captured in a tall page; it is not sufficient evidence of permanently inaccessible controls. Interactive scrolling remains untested."
    }
